# dataset/.gitignore
#
# Scoped to dataset/. Paths are relative to this file; works alongside the
# repo-root .gitignore (git applies both).
#
# ===========================================================================
# DESIGN RULE — read before adding anything here.
#
# Ignore by PATH, never by file extension.
#
# An extension says nothing about whether a file is a source or an output.
# A .pdf can be a re-fetchable bulk corpus OR a one-off report that exists
# nowhere else. A .zip can be a packaging artefact OR the only copy of a
# downloaded dataset. A .pkl can be a throwaway checkpoint OR the trained model
# the deployed engine loads at startup. Ignoring the extension gets the first
# case right and silently destroys the second.
#
# So: a rule belongs here only if a specific PATH is BOTH
#   (a) large, AND
#   (b) regenerable by a script committed in this repo.
# Both halves. If either fails, commit it.
#
# Default for anything new: COMMIT IT. This folder is evidence for an academic
# defence — a missing source file is far worse than a slightly larger repo.
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The DGHS daily dengue PDF corpus — 1,639 files, ~0.5-1 GB.
#
# Path-scoped deliberately: this is the ONE pdf location that is genuinely
# reproducible. raw/trauma/ and any future raw/<source>/ are NOT covered, and
# must not be — SOURCES.md already lists the DGHS Health Bulletin (robots-
# disallowed to automated fetch) and the BRTA/RSF reports as future sources.
# Those are PDFs that no script can re-fetch, so they have to be committed.
#
# Excluding these specific files does not weaken provenance:
#   - raw/dengue/_manifest.csv holds URL, HTTP status, bytes and SHA-256 for
#     every one of them, and IS committed (only *.pdf is excluded here).
#   - scripts/fetch_dengue_wayback.py re-fetches them deterministically from the
#     Wayback CDX API — resumable, idempotent, verifiable against those hashes.
#
# The SOURCES.md rule that raw files are NEVER EDITED BY HAND still holds
# absolutely. That is the half that actually protects the data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
raw/dengue/*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Diagnostic text dumps from parse_dengue.py --dump-text.
# Regenerable in seconds from any PDF; purely for calibrating extraction rules.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
reports/pdf_text/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicit scratch areas. Nothing here is ever an input to anything.
# Put throwaway experiments in these paths and they stay out of git by default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scratch/
tmp/
models/experiments/
notebooks/scratch/

# NOTE on trained models — deliberately NOT ignored.
# Stage 6B produces a forecasting model that the Python engine LOADS AT RUNTIME
# on Render to serve /forecast/risk-check. Retraining on a free-tier dyno is not
# viable, so the frozen model artefact must ship with the repo. A scikit-learn
# LinearRegression pickle is a few KB. Ignoring it would break the deployment.
# Only throwaway experiment runs go under models/experiments/ above.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. A future acquisition script (Kaggle, Mendeley, an API) will want one.
# .env.example is explicitly allowed back so the required keys stay documented.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
kaggle.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini